s><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit> </non-patent-citations> </citations> </technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ANDO KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI KANTA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORIUCHI KAZUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ZEXEL CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANDO, KOJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, KANTA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIUCHI, KAZUYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ZEXEL CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ANDO KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI KANTA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORIUCHI KAZUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANDO, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, KANTA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIUCHI, KAZUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A brushless motor includes protective means having a simple mechanism for protecting electronic components and so forth provided on a control board against both static electricity and heat of a heat sink. A protective member is provided which comprises integrated two mechanisms: a potential equalizing mechanism for equalizing the potential of the heat sink to the potential of one of power supply lines for a driving circuit disposed on the control board and a temperature fuse mechanism disposed on the control board. In consequence, static electricity generated in the heat sink can be made to flow to the circuit side and thereby the static electricity voltage is prevented from increasing. Therefore, temperature protection to cut off a circuit when temperature rises because of the heat from an electronic component (FET) attached to a heat sink is achieved by using only one member.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un moteur sans balais comprenant un dispositif de protection à mécanisme simple permettant de protéger les composants électroniques disposés sur un tableau de bord, contre à la fois l'électricité statique et la chaleur d'un dissipateur de chaleur. Par ailleurs, un élément de protection comprend deux mécanismes intégrés: un mécanisme égaliseur de potentiel permettant d'égaliser le potentiel du dissipateur de chaleur sur le potentiel de l'une des conduites d'alimentation d'un circuit d'attaque placé sur le tableau de bord, et un mécanisme à fusible thermique également disposé sur le tableau de bord. Ainsi, on peut amener l'électricité statique générée dans le dissipateur de chaleur à s'écouler du côté du circuit, empêchant ainsi la tension d'électricité statique d'augmenter. Par conséquent, on réalise la protection thermique contre la coupure de circuit due à l'augmentation de la température causée par la chaleur émanant d'un composant électronique (FET) fixé au dissipateur de chaleur, en n'utilisant qu'un seul élément.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>